INT. NEW BEGINNINGS FERTILITY CLINIC - WAITING ROOM - DAY

We see a quiet waiting room with beige chairs and a fish tank. The power has been out for three days after the storm, and the clinic is running on one generator. We can tell this because the lights are dim and the fish tank is not bubbling.

CLOSE ON a clock on the wall. It reads 2:14. It is not moving.

Maya, 30s, sits very straight with her purse in her lap. Beside her, Dev, 30s, is tapping his knee. They are not talking. We can tell they are not talking because there is no talking.

ON PHONE: Mom - where r u guys?? is it happening

Maya turns her phone face down on her thigh without answering.

A NURSE enters. We see that she is carrying a clipboard. She is young and looks like she has not slept since the storm began.

NURSE
Maya Rosen?

MAYA
Yes. That's me.

NURSE
Dr. Okafor will see you now. Only you, though. Generator rules.

DEV
(standing)
I'm her husband.

NURSE
I know, Mr. Rosen. I'm sorry.

Dev sits back down. He does not say anything. His hand is still on Maya's arm.

MAYA
Dev. It's okay.

DEV
(not meaning it)
Yeah. Okay.

Maya stands and follows the nurse through a swinging door. We see the door swing shut behind her.

Dev is alone. He pulls out his phone and we see the screen.

ON PHONE: Dev: they only let her in. what do i do

ON PHONE: Mom: sit. be there. thats the job

He looks at the fish tank. One fish is hanging at the surface, mouth opening and closing.

A WOMAN in a green raincoat enters from the street door. She is soaked. She looks at the empty reception desk, then at Dev, then back at the desk. She does not sign in.

DEV (CONT'D)
They're, uh... generator only. You might wait outside.

THE WOMAN
I'm not a patient.

DEV
Oh.

THE WOMAN
I'm here for the freezer.

DEV
What freezer?

She does not answer. She walks past him toward the hallway marked STAFF ONLY.

We see Dev watch her go. He stands, unsure, then follows at a distance.

INT. NEW BEGINNINGS FERTILITY CLINIC - HALLWAY - CONTINUOUS

The generator HUMS louder here. A row of steel tanks, each frosted with cold. The woman is already at the biggest one, pulling at its door.

DEV
Hey. Hey! You can't touch that.

THE WOMAN
The backup power's failing. Somebody has to move them.

DEV
Who are you?

THE WOMAN
Karen Ellis. Lab tech. Eleven years.

DEV
(quieter)
Karen. My wife's in there right now.

KAREN
Then you'd better help me lift.

He looks at the tank. At her. At the dark ceiling.

Dev takes off his jacket and grabs the other handle.

Behind them, the swinging door opens. Maya stands there, pale, with the nurse behind her.

MAYA
(very still)
Dev. What are you doing?

DEV
Saving the thing we came here for.

This is the first time all week that anyone in this building has told the truth.
